<article class="env-lemma" id="044D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/044D">Lemma <span data-tag="044D">78.17.3</span>.</a> The notions of restricting groupoids and (pre-)equivalence relations defined in Definitions <a href="/tag/044C" data-tag="044C">78.17.2</a> and <a href="/tag/043E" data-tag="043E">78.4.3</a> agree via the constructions of Lemmas <a href="/tag/043X" data-tag="043X">78.11.2</a> and <a href="/tag/043Y" data-tag="043Y">78.11.3</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      What we are saying here is that $R'$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/044B" data-tag="044B">78.17.1</a> is also equal to 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R' = (U' \times _ B U')\times _{U \times _ B U} R \longrightarrow U' \times _ B U'  \]
</div>
    <p>
       In fact this might have been a clearer way to state that lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>